  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 01f934d50526431a9392a6ceca1dc33d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rampage Cell Config 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  CellName: Rampage
  Description: Demolition arena cell, intensity 2 of 4 - a stirring arena: 59 seeded plants totalling
    ~9830 prisms of cacti, spires, pines, rosettes and coral, filling the volume from just
    outside the nucleus out to the membrane, across all three domains, each plant one of the
    four elemental variations. The PLANT AND PRISM COUNTS ARE THE SAME AT EVERY INTENSITY -
    what intensity changes is how BIG things are and how contested they get: prisms at 1.4x
    the authored leaf (bigger is an easier target for the cone and an easier surface to
    skim), a nucleus at prefab scale 400 (~392u radius), 2x the authored wildlife, and -
    authored in the scene, not here - one crystal per player. Intensity 4 is the shipped,
    play-tested arena exactly; 1 is the same arena made bigger and easier to hit. The
    nucleus stays clear (the planting band is clamped outside it) and is the crystals'
    contested ground. The mature forest is ~1,039,932 volume, and this cell's VOLUME
    thresholds are the play-tested intensity-4 ladder scaled by that - so Frenzy sits the
    same 4.11x above the forest at every level. Pending an in-editor re-measure; regenerate
    with Tools/Build/rampage_intensity.py rather than hand-editing.
